The terminal is a central tool in the workflow of both novice and professional developers, yet it often presents challenges due to its steep learning curve and overwhelming output.
To address these issues, we propose an AI-assisted system to enhance terminal usability.
Our approach is applied on a terminal, which is directly integrated into an IDE to be able to work within the context of a current development task. 
Outputs, such as those from a Java Build, are automatically processed by AI to filter redundant information and highlight the key points necessary for problem-solving.
In addition, the system recommends context-aware commands, helping users work more efficiently without memorizing extensive syntax.
Finally, by explaining commands, the system reduces time spent searching documentation and transforms errors into learning opportunities.
The primary focus lies on supporting students in educational settings, while the concepts explored here also point towards benefits for professional developers' workflows.
